{
  "version": 1,
  "generator": "tests/story_bench.c (make story)",
  "policy": "A pilot who reads the gauges, not the code: holds Raise (or Lower) until the apsis readout passes the target ring, releasing 3 % short to 8 % past it and 0-2 frames late; coasts until the tug is within 0-5 % of the ring, reacts after 0-5 frames and holds Match until the match error reads below 0.004-0.02; if the orbit turns before the ring, or nothing changes for 3 T, it circularizes or burns again. On the pod's ring it cuts the engine and waits. It does not smooth the wobbling readout. Its hand comes from the run's own stirred seed, re-drawn per leg. Choices follow the path field.",
  "crisis": "the tank gauge in the red (below 0.25) at any moment in the leg, or a failure (a failure counts as a crisis)",
  "failure": "the tank ran dry and a drone or Lamp Quay's tug had to come, the tug fell within 0.35 L of the star or wandered 45 T, or the pod's grapple glanced off",
  "segments": ["leaving the dock", "the climb to the buoy", "down below the flare front", "the flare", "the last leg"],
  "note": "16 seeds x 12 runs; every run has its own stirred seed; the path comes from the run number.",
